 use a communication protocol with a non-blocking write behavior, which is similar) Tj0 -14.04  TD -0.0078  Tc 0.0078  Tw (to the one in process networks.) Tj14.4 -14.04  TD -0.0036  Tc 0.7156  Tw (Another difference is on the level of abstraction. Since design is a process of refinement, the) Tj-14.4 -13.92  TD -0.0016  Tc 0.5034  Tw (description of a component may exist at different levels. In [ETT98], Eisenring,) Tj0  Tc 0  Tw ( ) Tj392.16 0  TD /F3 12  Tf0.48  Tw (et al.) Tj24.48 0  TD /F1 12  Tf-0.0027  Tc 0.4827  Tw ( divide the) Tj-416.64 -14.04  TD -0.0042  Tc 0.3882  Tw (possible abstractions into two levels: ) Tj181.8 0  TD /F3 12  Tf-0.0042  Tc 0.4842  Tw (abstract communication types) Tj144.84 0  TD /F1 12  Tf-0.016  Tc 0.256  Tw ( and ) Tj24.24 0  TD /F3 12  Tf-0.0051  Tc 0.4851  Tw (physical communication) Tj-350.88 -14.04  TD 0.012  Tc 0  Tw (types) Tj24.6 0  TD /F1 12  Tf-0.0051  Tc -0.1149  Tw (. Abstract communication types includes buffered versus non-buffered, blocking versus non-) Tj-24.6 -13.92  TD -0.002  Tc 3.842  Tw (blocking, synchronous versus asynchronous communication. Physical communication types) Tj0 -14.04  TD -0.0026  Tc 1.3676  Tw (includes memory-mapped I/O, interrupt or DMA-transfer. In [BLO98], Borriello,) Tj0  Tc 0  Tw ( ) Tj406.2 0  TD /F3 12  Tf1.44  Tw (et al.) Tj25.44 0  TD /F1 12  Tf0.006  Tc 1.314  Tw ( gave ) Tj1.272  Tc 0  Tw (a) Tj-431.64 -14.04  TD 0  Tc 1.5833  Tw (more contiguous categorization of interface levels: electrical, logical, sequencing, timing, data) Tj0 -13.92  TD -0.0049  Tc 1.4449  Tw (transaction, packet, and message. The behavioral type work addresses the highest level in this) Tj0 -14.04  TD -0  Tc 1.2121  Tw (classification: different mechanisms for message passing. It covers the abstract communication) TjT* -0.0034  Tc 0.4234  Tw (types. On the other hand, most work on protocol synthesis is at the hardware or architecture lev-) Tj0 -13.92  TD -0.0011  Tc 0.5291  Tw (els. For example, reconfigurable computing with FPGA is targeted in [EiP00];) Tj0  Tc 0  Tw ( ) Tj385.2 0  TD 0.0137  Tc 0.4663  Tw ([PRS98] is about) Tj-385.2 -14.04  TD -0.0019  Tc 0.7403  Tw (RTL level interface synthesis; the problem of mapping a high-level specification to an architec-) Tj0 -14.04  TD -0.0013  Tc -0.1787  Tw (ture is considered in ) Tj98.88 0  TD -0.0035  Tc -0.2365  Tw ([OrB97]; and a system to generate interface between a set of microprocessors) Tj-98.88 -13.92  TD -0.0033  Tc 0.0033  Tw (and a set of devices is described in [COB92]) Tj213.84 0  TD 0.027  Tc 0  Tw ([COB95].) Tj-199.44 -14.04  TD -0.0051  Tc 0.4165  Tw (The differences between our type system and the work in protocol synthesis make them com-) Tj-14.4 -14.04  TD -0.0023  Tc 0.0023  Tw (plementary to each other. They may be used at the different stages of the design process.) Tj0 -29.28  TD /F2 13.92  Tf0.0457  Tc -0.0754  Tw (7. Conclusion and Future Work) Tj0 -18.72  TD /F1 12  Tf-0.0013  Tc 0.4536  Tw (We have proposed two extensions to the interface automata formalism. Transient states allow us) Tj0 -13.92  TD -0.0037  Tc 0.0692  Tw (to model mutual exclusion easily, and projection automata expose alternating simulation between) Tj0 -14.04  TD -0.0058  Tc 0.0058  Tw (two automata for a subset of their interfaces.) Tj14.4 -14.04  TD -0.0037  Tc 0.6723  Tw (Based on the extended interface automata, we have described a type system that captures the) Tj-14.4 -13.92  TD -0.0036  Tc 0.6145  Tw (interaction dynamics in a component-based design environment. The interaction types and com-) Tj0 -14.04  TD 0.0012  Tc -0.0658  Tw (ponent behavior are described by interface automata, and type checking is done through automata) TjT* -0.0042  Tc 0.5119  Tw (composition. Our approach is domain polymorphic in that a component may be compatible with) Tj0 -13.92  TD 0.0016  Tc 1.0046  Tw (multiple interaction types. The relation among the interaction types is captured by a behavioral) Tj0 -14.04  TD -0.0019  Tc -0.1696  Tw (type order using the alternating simulation relation of interface automata. We have shown that our) TjT* -0.0035  Tc -0.1315  Tw (system can be extended to capture more dynamic properties, and the design of a good type system) Tj0 -13.92  TD -0.0025  Tc 0.2939  Tw (involves a set of trade-offs. Our experimental platform is the Ptolemy II design environment. All) Tj0 -14.04  TD -0.0032  Tc -0.2668  Tw (the automata in this paper are built in Ptolemy II and their compositions are computed in software,) TjT* -0.0047  Tc 0.0047  Tw (except that some manual layout is applied for better readability of the diagrams.) TjETendstreamendobj252 0 obj6680endobj250 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 247 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F1 8 0 R /F2 12 0 R /F3 14 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 251 0 R>>endobj254 0 obj<</Length 255 0 R>>stream
